# Dependabot PR Workflow

Use this rule when the user asks to "handle dependabot PRs", "update dependencies", or "process dependabot".

Full guide: [docs/guides/dependabot-process.md](../../docs/guides/dependabot-process.md).

## Autonomous mode (default)

When the user asks to handle/process Dependabot PRs, **run the full queue end-to-end without asking for confirmation at each step**. Only stop to report blockers (failed CI, conflicts after rebase, risky/RN-upgrade PRs).

**Do not merge** non-Dependabot PRs (e.g. chore workflow PR #60) unless the user explicitly includes them.

### Queue loop

1. List open Dependabot PRs: `gh pr list --search "author:app/dependabot state:open" --json number,title,mergeable,mergeStateStatus,statusCheckRollup,files`
2. Triage each PR (safe / risky / skip / RN upgrade).
3. **Parallel prep**: comment `@dependabot rebase` on every open bot that is `CONFLICTING`, has stale CI (>24h), or is not the PR about to merge — **skip** PRs with `IN_PROGRESS` CI that Dependabot already refreshed after the last `main` merge.
4. Pick the **oldest safe PR** with all required checks `SUCCESS` and `mergeable: MERGEABLE`.
5. `gh pr review <N> --approve` then `gh pr merge <N> --squash --delete-branch`.
6. Wait for `main` CI green: Lint Check, Test Check, Quality Gates (`gh run list --branch main --limit 5`).
7. Go to step 3 until no safe PRs remain. Write batch notes in a PR/issue comment; land `docs/guides/dependabot-resolution-log.md` via a **ticketed chore PR** (never commit on `main`).

### CI-first merge gate (safe PRs)

For **safe** PRs (lockfile-only / non-native patch bumps; no native or Expo ecosystem `package.json` changes):

- Required GitHub checks green is enough — **local `npm ci` + doctor optional**.
- Required checks: Lint & Format, Unit Tests, Quality Gates (TypeScript, lockfile expo-doctor, expo install --check) — all `SUCCESS`.
- Branch protection requires approval: always `gh pr review --approve` before merge.

For **risky** / native / Expo ecosystem bumps: local `npm ci` + doctor + full CI gate + Android smoke still mandatory.

**GitHub Actions** SHA bumps (`github_actions` label): merge when Action pins check + required checks are green — **do not skip by default** (match historical merge of Actions SHA bumps).

### Skip without merge

- Any required check `FAILURE` or `CANCELLED` (including **Expo Doctor** / SDK version mismatch)
- `mergeable: CONFLICTING` after `@dependabot rebase` (retry rebase once; then report)
- RN line upgrade or pinned React/RN drift (also covered by `dependabot.yml` ignores — see `.github/dependabot.yml`)
- `@op-engineering/op-sqlite` major bump
- Deferred majors (Jest 30, Babel 8, ESLint 10, lucide v1, etc.): close only when an ignore rule will hold them **or** a dedicated upgrade ticket is opened/linked — no orphan “needs ticket” comments

### Useful commands

    gh pr checks <N> --watch          # wait for CI
    gh pr comment <N> --body "@dependabot rebase"
    gh run list --branch main --limit 3 --json workflowName,conclusion,status

## CRITICAL SAFETY RULES

1. **Verify author**: ONLY process PRs authored by `app/dependabot` or `dependabot[bot]`.
2. **Never auto-merge React Native line bumps**: If a PR upgrades `react-native` past the pinned `0.86.x` line or multiple `@react-native/*` packages together, DO NOT merge. Plan a dedicated RN upgrade ticket.
3. **Mandatory validation (tiered)**: **Safe** lockfile-only / non-native patches may merge on required GitHub checks alone (CI-first). **Risky** / native / Expo ecosystem bumps: NEVER merge without local `npm ci` + `npm run doctor` + the full gate from [commands.mdc](./commands.mdc): `format:check` → `lint` → `typecheck` → `npm test -- --ci` (and Android smoke). Quality Gates on the PR still must be green either way.
4. **Target branch**: Dependabot PRs merge into `main` via GitHub squash-merge only. **Agent-authored changes** (expo doctor CI, lockfile fixes, resolution-log catch-up) never push to `main` — separate ticketed PR ([delivery.mdc](./delivery.mdc)).
5. **Version lock-stepping**: `react`, `react-dom`, `react-test-renderer`, and `react-native` are pinned for Expo SDK 57 / RN 0.86 (`dependabot.yml` ignores all React updates). Treat any change to those as **risky** — validate on device/emulator; prefer a dedicated ticket over merging a bot.
6. **Runtime testing required**: For React/RN/navigation/native-module updates, smoke test on Android (`npm run android`). Static checks miss renderer and native ABI mismatches.
7. **Manual merges = high risk**: Prefer `@dependabot rebase`. If manual merge is required, run full validation + Android smoke test.
8. **Final state validation**: After merging multiple PRs, ALWAYS validate the final merged state on `main`.
9. **One Dependabot merge at a time (lockfile)**: Merge **at most one** lockfile PR, wait for **`main` CI green**, then **`@dependabot rebase` all other open bots in parallel** (prep while CI runs on the ones already rebased). Never stack merges without rebasing — corrupt `package-lock.json` breaks `npm ci`.
10. **Deferred upgrades**: When closing a bot as “needs dedicated ticket”, open/link that ticket **or** rely on the ignore rules in `.github/dependabot.yml` — do not leave orphan “needs ticket” comments with no tracker.

## Implementation workflow

### Step 1: Triage and categorize

Fetch open Dependabot PRs:

```bash
gh pr list --author app/dependabot --author dependabot[bot] --state open --json number,title,author
```

Categorize each PR:

- **Safe**: Lockfile-only / non-native patch bumps; GitHub Actions SHA bumps with Action pins + required checks green.
- **Risky**: `react`, `react-native`, `@react-native/*`, `@react-navigation/*`, `@op-engineering/op-sqlite`, Expo ecosystem, or any native-linked package — local doctor + Android smoke.
- **RN upgrade / ignored majors**: `react-native` `>=0.87`, React pin drift, Jest/Babel/ESLint/lucide majors covered by ignores. **Action: close with explanation** — open/link a dedicated ticket **or** confirm the ignore rule will hold (no orphan closes).

### Step 2: Validation for each PR

**Safe (CI-first):** confirm required GitHub checks are `SUCCESS` — local checkout optional.

**Risky / native / Expo:** local checkout is mandatory:

1. **Checkout**:

   ```bash
   git fetch origin pull/<PR_NUMBER>/head:dependabot-pr-<PR_NUMBER>
   git checkout dependabot-pr-<PR_NUMBER>
   npm ci
   ```

2. **Technical validation** (CI order):

   ```bash
   npm run doctor          # Expo SDK / RN duplicate-module alignment — fails fast on bad rebases
   npm run format:check
   npm run lint
   npm run typecheck
   npm test -- --ci
   ```

   If `npm run doctor` fails with patch mismatches caused by **this** bot, run `npx expo install --fix` on the PR branch, then re-run the suite. If `--check` is red overnight with no change in this PR, wait for #422 and rebase. Do **not** merge until doctor/`--check` are clean.

   *Note: `fluent-api.test.ts` may hit the network — a failure there alone does not block a dep bump if it also fails on `main`.*

3. **Native build** (optional locally for risky PRs; CI uses EAS preview when needed):

   ```bash
   npm run prebuild
   cd android && ./gradlew assembleDebug --no-daemon && cd ..
   ```

4. **Smoke test (mandatory for React/RN/navigation/native modules)**:

   ```bash
   npm start   # separate terminal
   npm run android
   ```

   **Check**:

   - App launches without crashes
   - No "Incompatible React versions" errors
   - Navigation: Projects → Chapters → Verse detail
   - Sync button still runs without throwing

### Step 3: Merging

If CI-first (safe) or local validation (risky) passes:

    gh pr review <PR_NUMBER> --approve --body "CI green. Safe lockfile bump per dependabot workflow."
    gh pr merge <PR_NUMBER> --squash --delete-branch

Wait for `main` CI green. **Immediately** rebase all other open bots in parallel (do not wait for the next merge candidate):

    for n in $(gh pr list --search "author:app/dependabot state:open" --json number -q '.[].number'); do
      gh pr comment "$n" --body "@dependabot rebase"
    done

Skip rebasing the PR whose CI is already `IN_PROGRESS` from a recent Dependabot push. Repeat from triage for the next green PR.

### Step 4: Final validation on main

**CRITICAL**: After merging multiple PRs, validate the **final merged state**:

```bash
git checkout main
git pull origin main
npm ci
npm run doctor
npm run format:check
npm run lint
npm run typecheck
npm test -- --ci
cd android && ./gradlew assembleDebug --no-daemon && cd ..
```

Optional but recommended after risky merges: `npm run android` smoke test.

**Why**: Individual PRs may pass, but combined merges can create incompatibilities (e.g. React patch drift vs pinned `react-test-renderer`).

### Step 5: Cleanup

```bash
git branch -D dependabot-pr-<PR_NUMBER>
```

## Handling issues

### Conflicts

**Prefer**: Comment `@dependabot rebase` on the PR.

```bash
gh pr comment <PR_NUMBER> --body "@dependabot rebase"
```

**If manual resolution required** (high risk):

1. Do not automatically choose "newer" versions for `react` / `react-native` / `@react-native/*`
2. Run the full validation suite + Android smoke test after resolving
3. Consider requesting user approval before merging

### Version mismatches

Expo SDK 57 / RN 0.86.3 pins these in `package.json` — verify after any manual conflict resolution:

| Package | Current pin |
|---------|-------------|
| `react` | `19.2.3` |
| `react-native` | `0.86.3` |
| `react-test-renderer` | `19.2.3` |
| `@react-native/jest-preset` | `0.86.3` |
| `@react-native/typescript-config` | `0.86.3` |

Bump `@react-native/jest-preset` and `@react-native/typescript-config` together with `react-native` — RN peers the jest preset at the exact patch, so a lone `react-native` bump fails `npm install` with `ERESOLVE`.

If a Dependabot PR drifts these, align manually to the [React Native upgrade helper](https://react-native-community.github.io/upgrade-helper/?from=0.86.3&to=0.86.3) matrix before merging.

### Failures

- **Expo Doctor fails**: Do not merge. Run `npx expo install --check`; if mismatches are SDK patch drift, `npx expo install --fix` on the PR branch. For duplicate native modules, see [Expo FYI: resolving dependency issues](https://github.com/expo/fyi/blob/main/resolving-dependency-issues.md) (`npm why`, `npm dedupe`, `overrides`).
- **Tests fail**: Do not merge. Share logs with user.
- **Lint / format fail**: Do not merge. Share logs with user.
- **`npm ci` fails on `main`**: Usually corrupted `package-lock.json` from stacked merges — regenerate with `npm install`, open a small fix PR.
- **Runtime crash**: Check React/RN version alignment and native module compatibility (`@op-engineering/op-sqlite`, etc.).

